	<strings name="main_menu/settings_select/player_setup/player_profile_edit/mods_settings/help_strings">
		<string text="Texture, sound, text and model packs from the mods folder, and the Theater's recorded games."/>
		<string text=""/>
		<string text="Texture, sound, text and model packs from the mods folder: turn each on or off, and choose which plays over which. They are this computer's, for every profile."/>
		<string text="Each mod is a folder in the mods folder, beside the maps folder, with its mod.toml and its tags. Mods are turned on and off from the main menu's Settings, not in a game."/>
		<string text=""/>
		<string text="Records each network game you play or host, from the next one on, to watch again in the Theater."/>
		<string text="The games recorded: watch one again from any player's view, or a free or cinematic camera."/>
		<string text=""/>
		<string text="Gives weapons and armour the fine grain of their surfaces (machining, weave, wear) from a mod's material overlay. It changes only the light on them. Off draws them as the Xbox did."/>
		<string text="Characters, weapons and vehicles catch the level's own lights as highlights, where their armour is shiny. Off draws them as the Xbox did."/>
		<string text="Local: shiny armour reflects the place it is in, captured on this computer from your maps. Classic reflects the game's own painted reflections."/>
		<string text="Characters shade themselves and each other from the level's main light. Needs ambient occlusion World. Classic keeps the Xbox's shadows alone."/>
		<string text="Remodel draws the level's rock, sand and Forerunner walls from a denser model built on this computer from your maps: rounded rock, bevelled edges, the same light. You still walk and collide on the original. Xbox draws the map's own."/>
		<string text=""/>
		<string text="Smooth: the levels' own light drawn without its colour bands and blocky edges, from a finer copy built on this machine the first time a level is played. The light stays where it was."/>
		<string text="A soft glow about light brighter than white: plasma, the sun, lights and blasts. The Xbox had none; Glow is faint, Full wider. Nothing lit only to white glows."/>
	</strings>
